      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(runtime): harden provider process cleanup",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nKova could trust stale or recycled PID files, signal unrelated processes, discard retry state before a provider actually stopped, and overwrite diagnostic artifacts that shared a basename.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n- Validate every diagnostic and mock-provider PID as a positive integer before interpolation or signaling.\n- Authenticate the complete mock-provider command line against the expected executable, script, port, and request log.\n- Retain PID files when inspection, signaling, or confirmed shutdown fails so cleanup remains retryable.\n- Stop failed mock-provider launches before returning failure.\n- Remove terminal PID files only after absence or confirmed shutdown.\n- Hash diagnostic artifact source paths so same-basename files remain distinct.\n- Add self-check coverage for invalid, recycled, mismatched, delayed-exit, timeout, trailing-argument, failed-launch, and artifact-collision cases.\n\n## User Impact\n\nKova cleanup no longer risks terminating an unrelated process from stale PID state. Failed or delayed provider shutdowns remain visible and retryable, while diagnostic collection preserves every distinct artifact.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `NO_COLOR=1 npm run check`\n  - concurrent self-check isolation: pass\n  - Kova self-check: 233/233 passed in 46.2s\n- Sol/high autoreview over the complete branch: clean, confidence 0.91\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD`\n- Five scoped commits retained; no squash.\n",
